tting-tips/Rugby_Union/All_Rugby_Union/All_Events/Six_Nations_2027/9?event_id=609013",[752,756,759,762],{"title":753,"theme":754,"side_image":43,"sections_content":755},"Six Nations Tips on OLBG","default","\u003Cp>Rugby tips on OLBG are growing, and the year's highlight is this Six Nations tournament. Tipsters have added their Six Nations tips for the tournament winner above and can also bet on individual match markets, with handicap betting very popular.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Six Nations predictions for other betting markets, which also include double results, winning margin and highest-scoring half, can be viewed on the individual \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Rugby_Union/9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Six Nations match tips\u003C/a> page.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>You can check which rugby tipsters to follow as we record and analyse their performance. By each tip, you can read why that tipster is recommending a bet. You can see how knowledgeable the tipster is by the comments they are making on their predictions.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>We also show you the rugby tipsters' profit or loss over the past week, month and year for their Rugby Union tips and how consistent they are with their picks by way of strike rate.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>To check out how the rugby tipsters compare against others in the current month, up to the past year, visit the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/tipsters/tables?id=c-139\">Rugby tipping table\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If you fancy yourself as a rugby tipster, we offer a standalone \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/members/make-tip/9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Six Nations tipping competition\u003C/a> with a prize fund of £200 for the best rugby tipsters. It's a simple way to show the world your tipping prowess, and you could win some instant cash! The comp runs for the entire duration of the Six Nations tournament.\u003C/p>",{"title":757,"theme":754,"side_image":43,"sections_content":758},"Six Nations Betting from OLBG","\u003Cp>The Six Nations pre-tournament betting odds currently available show that, alongside each team, these odds will fluctuate when the tournament gets underway.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If you find a tipster and Six Nations tip to your liking, to place a bet, just click the 'Add' to betslip icon directly below the odds for your chosen selection.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>As soon as you do this, you will be able to check which bookmaker has the best Six Nations odds for your pick. Then select the bookie with the best odds, and you will instantly go to the chosen bookmaker. It's a simple way to bet.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If you do not have a bookmaker account or wish to check \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/bookmakers/articles/best-bookmakers-for-rugby-betting \">which is the best bookmaker for rugby betting,&nbsp;\u003C/a>our guide will assist you with all your Rugby betting questions. Just click the link.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Rugby betting is of growing interest, with the bookies offering more betting markets; there may not be as many as football, but they are at least giving us more choices these days.\u003C/p>",{"title":760,"theme":754,"side_image":43,"sections_content":761},"Six Nations Format and Past Winners","\u003Cp>The Six Nations Rugby tournament is contested annually by England, Scotland, the Republic of Ireland, Wales, France and Italy. The competition has been in its current format since 2000, when Italy first took part. The six countries play one game against each other, with home-ground advantage alternating each year.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The points system is open to amendment, but as of 2026:\u003C/p>\u003Cul type=\"disc\">\u003Cli>A win is 4 points, or if the country scores four tries or more, 5 points.\u003C/li>\u003Cli>If the losing country scores four tries or more, OR by a margin of seven points or fewer, it scores 1 point.\u003C/li>\u003Cli>If the losing country scores four tries or more AND loses by a margin of seven points or fewer, it scores 2 points.\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Countries that draw a game shall each be awarded 2 points; any of them that score four tries or more in the process shall be awarded a further 1 point.\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cp>For a detailed guide, head over to our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/blogs/six-nations-betting-preview\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Six Nations blog\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch4>Six Nations Winners\u003C/h4>\u003Cp>The most successful countries during the Six Nations era (2000 onwards) are France, who won their eighth title in 2026, moving them one clear of England on seven wins. Just one behind England with six wins are Wales and Ireland, whilst both Scotland and Italy are yet to win the Six Nations.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>A country that wins all five of its matches wins the “Grand Slam”.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If a home nation (England, Ireland, Scotland, Wales) beats each of its rivals, they win the “Triple Crown”.\u003C/p>\u003Ch4>The last Ten Six Nations winners:\u003C/h4>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth width=\"10%\">Year\u003C/th>\u003Cth width=\"30%\">Winners\u003C/th>\u003Cth width=\"30%\">Grand Slam?\u003C/th>\u003Cth width=\"30%\">Triple Crown?\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2026\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>France\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2025\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>France\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2024\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2023\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2022\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>France\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>France\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2021\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Wales\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Wales\u003Cbr>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2020\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>England\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>England\u003Cbr>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2019\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Wales\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Wales\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Wales\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2018\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Ireland\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>2017\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>England\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>",{"title":43,"theme":754,"side_image":43,"sections_content":763},"\u003Cp>Luke Bradshaw Lee and Darren Brett, the driving forces behind OLBG's dynamic Rugby Union content, merge to deliver an immersive experience for fans. With Luke's passion spanning both Rugby League and Rugby Union and Darren's understanding of the sport, their collaboration offers comprehensive insights, betting strategies, and in-depth analysis for the Six Nations.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-olbg-light-blue rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-bleu  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/luke-bradshaw-lee\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098785434.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098785434.jpeg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"Luke Bradshaw Lee\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/eca/4c4/649eca4c4e5c2098